    "expensive_path": "Per-step phonon kinematics: G4CMPPhononKinematics solves the 3x3 Christoffel eigenproblem (or reads the K-Vg lookup table) for every phonon step to map wavevector to group velocity and polarization; examples/caustics propagates 40,000,000 ballistic phonons this way (173 s single-thread as shipped) and is embarrassingly parallel across events, as are the isotope-scattering and downconversion loops of examples/phonon.",
    "rationale": "One physics: acoustic phonons in an anisotropic crystal. The processes (G4PhononScattering, G4PhononDownconversion, G4CMPPhononBoundaryProcess), their rates, the kinematics tables and the two phonon examples form a closed set that needs no charge or quasiparticle code.",
    "excluded": [
      "Luke phonon emission by drifting carriers (a charge-carrier process; its phonons use this module's transport once produced)",
      "Polycrystalline elastic scattering in superconducting films and phonon radiation by quasiparticles (kept with the quasiparticle module because their only official tests are the validation suite)",
      "Phonon hits digitisation by electrodes beyond G4CMPPhononElectrode (examples/sensors, not packaged)"
    ],
    "hazards": [
      "No random seed is set anywhere; reruns are bit-identical only through Geant4's default engine state, and a port that changes the number or order of random draws breaks pointwise comparison",
      "examples/phonon and examples/caustics open hits files in append mode; a check must start from a clean directory",
      "caustics at the shipped 40,000,000 events takes about 3 min single-thread; the event count is the runtime knob",
      "examples/phonon/README is stale 2012 text (describes caustic.ssv, timing.ssv, XGeBox that do not exist)"
    ]
  },
